          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "let reviews = [\n  {\n    \"price\": \"$$\",          \n    \"stars\": \"5\",\n    \"wait\": \"30\",\n    \"recommend\": \"yes\",\n    \"name\": \"Joe's Diner\",\n    \"type\": \"casual\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"price\": \"cheap\",\n    \"stars\": \"4/5\",\n    \"wait\": \"15-20\",\n    \"recommend\": \"no\",\n    \"name\": \"Maria's Cafe\", \n    \"type\": \"cafe\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"price\": \"$$$\", \n    \"stars\": \"8\",\n    \"wait\": \"reservation\",\n    \"recommend\": \"yes\",\n    \"name\": \"Nathan Sanchez\",\n    \"type\": \"formal\"\n  }\n];",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "1"
      ]
    },
    "long_instructions": "## Investigate Misleading Schema\r\n\r\nThe product review data has inconsistent field names and data types. Your job is to figure out what's unclear and fix it so the data means the same thing to everyone — including AI.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Look at the `reviews` dataset in `script.js`. What do you notice about the field names and values?\r\n\r\n2. Share the dataset with AI Tutor and ask it to identify anything confusing or inconsistent about the field names and data types.\r\n\r\n3. Review AI's response. Do you agree with what it flagged? Is there anything it missed?\r\n\r\n4. Update the `reviews` dataset — rename unclear fields and standardize inconsistent values.\r\n\r\n5. Share your updated dataset with AI Tutor and ask whether the schema is now consistent and clear.\r\n\r\n",
